.Dd $Mdocdate: October 24 2026 $
.Dt OPENBARRC 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openbarrc
.Nd openbar status bar configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This manual page describes the
.Xr openbar 1
configuration file.
.Pp
The configuration syntax follows the keyword style of
.Xr cwm 1 ,
with directives separated by whitespace from their arguments.
A hash mark
.Pq Sq #
starts a comment only at the beginning of a line, after optional
whitespace; there are no inline comments.
The values of
.Ic logo
and
.Ic fontname ,
and the colour name in
.Ic color ,
extend to the end of the line and may contain spaces without quotes.
A single matching pair of double
.Pq \&"
or single
.Pq '
quotes around the whole value is optional and preserves leading or
trailing whitespace; there is no escape syntax, and a quoted value
must not be followed by other characters.
Other directives take unquoted arguments; quoting is not stripped
from them.
.Pp
The file is UTF-8 encoded and text values such as
.Ic logo
may contain arbitrary Unicode characters.
The parser does not validate UTF-8; invalid byte sequences are passed
through to Xft.
Keyword and widget names, diagnostics and all other interface text are
U.S. English only; locale environment variables have no effect on the
syntax.
Colour names are limited to 63 bytes.
.Pp
The following options are accepted:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic barheight Ar pixels
Set the height of the status bar in pixels, between 12 and 60.
The default is 24.
A value larger than the screen height is clamped at runtime.
.It Ic color barbg Ar color
Set the background colour of the bar.
The default is
.Dq #CCCCCC
.Pq the cwm active border colour .
.It Ic color barfg Ar color
Set the foreground
.Pq text
colour of the bar.
The default is
.Dq #000000 .
.It Ic color urgent Ar color
Set the colour used for urgent elements (currently the battery
segment at or below 15% charge).
The default is
.Dq #FC8814
.Pq the cwm urgency border colour .
.It Ic fontname Ar font
Set the font used for bar text.
The
.Ar font
argument is an
.Xr Xft 3
font pattern.
The default is
.Dq sans-serif:pixelsize=14:bold
.Pq the same default font as cwm .
.It Ic gap Ar top bottom left right
Define gaps in pixels for the four screen edges.
Exactly four non-negative values are required.
The top, left, and right values position the top-edge bar window,
which is not managed by the window manager.
The bottom value is accepted for cwm-style symmetry and currently does
not affect the bar, which is anchored to the top edge.
The default is
.Dq 0 0 0 0 .
Left and right gaps that leave no usable width (their sum is at least
the screen width) are fatal.
.It Ic interface Ar name
Set the preferred network interface name used to read the interface
IPv4 address.
If the interface does not exist, is down, or has no IPv4 address, the
first usable non-loopback interface is used instead.
The selected address is not range-checked, so an interface can supply a
public IPv4 address here.
The name must be at most 15 bytes, must begin with a letter or an
underscore, and may otherwise contain letters, digits, underscore,
dash and dot.
.It Ic logo Ar text
Set the text displayed as the bar logo, at most 127 bytes.
This field is required.
The limit counts bytes, so multibyte UTF-8 characters consume more
than one byte.
.It Ic show Ar widget
Enable the given status widget.
.It Ic hide Ar widget
Disable the given status widget.
.El
.Pp
Available widget names for
.Ic show
and
.Ic hide :
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It hostname
System hostname.
.It date
Current date and time.
.It cpu
CPU clock speed and temperature.
.It mem
Free physical memory in MiB.
.It load
1-minute load average.
.It bat
Battery charge percentage.
.It vpn
WireGuard VPN status.
.It net
Public IPv4, IPv6 and interface IPv4 addresses.
.El
.Pp
Widgets render in the order listed above.
.Pp
All widgets are disabled by default.
When a directive occurs several times, the last occurrence wins.
An unknown keyword with an argument is reported and ignored; an
unknown keyword without an argument is treated as a missing argument
and is fatal.
Malformed numeric values, missing arguments, unknown widget names,
unknown colour slots, invalid interface names, overlong lines, and a
missing
.Ic logo
are fatal errors.
Colour names and font patterns are not syntax-checked at parse time;
unusable values are reported and replaced with defaults when X11 is
initialized.
Parse diagnostics include the file name and line number; I/O errors and
the missing-logo error include the file name.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.openbarrc" -compact
.It Pa ~/.openbarrc
Default per-user configuration file.
.It Pa /etc/openbarrc
System-wide configuration file.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
# Minimal openbar configuration
fontname "sans-serif:pixelsize=14:bold"
color barbg "#CCCCCC"
color barfg "#000000"
color urgent "#FC8814"
barheight 24
gap 0 0 0 0
logo OpenBar
interface iwm0
show hostname
show date
show cpu
show mem
show load
show vpn
show net
hide bat
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cwm 1 ,
.Xr openbar 1 ,
.Xr Xft 3 ,
.Xr cwmrc 5
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
file format first appeared in
.Ox .
